#: src/scans/on_access_page/on_access_presentation.rs:284
msgid "On-access blocking"
msgstr ""

#: src/scans/on_access_page/on_access_presentation.rs:286
msgid ""
"clamonacc checks files in the watched folders as they are opened. With "
"prevention on, the kernel refuses access to a detected file, which is why "
"such a file can't be opened even though it is still there."
msgstr ""

#: src/scans/on_access_page/on_access_presentation.rs:328
msgid "Mount watching"
msgstr ""

#: src/scans/on_access_page/on_access_presentation.rs:330
msgid ""
"OnAccessMountPath watches a whole mount through fanotify. ClamAV documents "
"it as incompatible with OnAccessPrevention, OnAccessIncludePath, "
"OnAccessExcludePath and OnAccessExtraScanning, so detected files on a "
"watched mount are never blocked. Watch folders with OnAccessIncludePath to "
"block."
msgstr ""

#: src/scans/on_access_page/on_access_presentation.rs:335
#, rust-format
msgid "OnAccessMountPath can't be combined with {options}"
msgstr ""

#: src/scans/on_access_page/on_access_presentation.rs:339
msgid "Scan loop protection"
msgstr ""

#: src/scans/on_access_page/on_access_presentation.rs:341
msgid ""
"clamd opens every file it is asked to scan. Unless OnAccessExcludeUname or "
"OnAccessExcludeUID names the user clamd runs as, clamonacc sees those reads "
"and asks clamd to scan the same files again."
msgstr ""

#: src/scans/on_access_page/on_access_presentation.rs:345
msgid "clamd isn't excluded, so clamonacc can scan its own reads endlessly"
msgstr ""

#: src/scans/on_access_page/on_access_presentation.rs:348
msgid "Watching the whole file system"
msgstr ""

#: src/scans/on_access_page/on_access_presentation.rs:350
msgid ""
"clamonacc refuses OnAccessIncludePath /. Include the folders that receive "
"files, such as home directories, or watch a mount with OnAccessMountPath."
msgstr ""

#: src/scans/on_access_page/on_access_presentation.rs:353
msgid "OnAccessIncludePath / is rejected by clamonacc"
msgstr ""

#: src/scans/on_access_page/on_access_presentation.rs:359
#: src/scans/on_access_page/on_access_presentation.rs:371
msgid "Folder watch limit"
msgstr ""

#: src/scans/on_access_page/on_access_presentation.rs:362
#, rust-format
msgid ""
"{path} is watched, but fs.inotify.max_user_watches is only {limit}, so "
"folders past the limit go unchecked"
msgstr ""

#: src/scans/on_access_page/on_access_presentation.rs:374
#, rust-format
msgid ""
